From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 04:04:01 +0200
Subject: ARM: dts: allwinner: sun8i-a83t-tbs-a711: Add DCDC ramp delays

The AXP813 walks its bucks to a new voltage in steps whenever DVM is
enabled, which it is out of reset for DCDC2..7 (REG 27H defaults to
FCH), at 2.5 mV/us for the 3 MHz buck frequency the driver programs
when the device tree does not ask for another one.

Nothing told the regulator core about that, so regulator_set_voltage()
returned as soon as the RSB write had landed and cpufreq took the new
CPU clock while the rail was still on its way up.  Give the four bucks
that have a voltage range here the rate from the datasheet; DCDC1 has
no DVM at all and DCDC6 is fixed.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-a83t-tbs-a711.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-a83t-tbs-a711.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-a83t-tbs-a711.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-a83t-tbs-a711.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-a83t-tbs-a711.dts
@@ -612,6 +612,7 @@ &reg_dcdc1 {
 &reg_dcdc2 {
 	regulator-min-microvolt = <700000>;
 	regulator-max-microvolt = <1100000>;
+	regulator-ramp-delay = <2500>;
 	regulator-always-on;
 	regulator-name = "vdd-cpu-A";
 };
@@ -619,6 +620,7 @@ &reg_dcdc2 {
 &reg_dcdc3 {
 	regulator-min-microvolt = <700000>;
 	regulator-max-microvolt = <1100000>;
+	regulator-ramp-delay = <2500>;
 	regulator-always-on;
 	regulator-name = "vdd-cpu-B";
 };
@@ -626,12 +628,14 @@ &reg_dcdc3 {
 &reg_dcdc4 {
 	regulator-min-microvolt = <700000>;
 	regulator-max-microvolt = <1100000>;
+	regulator-ramp-delay = <2500>;
 	regulator-name = "vdd-gpu";
 };
 
 &reg_dcdc5 {
 	regulator-min-microvolt = <1200000>;
 	regulator-max-microvolt = <1500000>;
+	regulator-ramp-delay = <2500>;
 	regulator-always-on;
 	regulator-name = "vcc-dram";
 };
